Third-party software installed when building the container images
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Dockerfiles in this repository (apps/api, apps/web,
packages/core/docker/skill-sandbox.Dockerfile) download and install
third-party software at build time. That software is not part of this
repository and is distributed under its own license terms, including:

  - Python packages pinned in apps/api/requirements.docker.txt and
    packages/core/docker/requirements.sandbox*.txt (from uv.lock)
  - npm packages pinned in pnpm-lock.yaml
  - Debian packages from the base images, including fonts-nanum
    (SIL Open Font License 1.1) in the skill sandbox image
  - Node.js (MIT) in the web and skill sandbox images

Notable non-permissive licenses among the runtime dependencies (unmodified,
used as libraries): certifi, orjson, tqdm, dompurify (MPL-2.0, or a choice
including it), tld (MPL-1.1 / GPL-2.0 / LGPL-2.1 tri-license),
@img/sharp-libvips-* (LGPL-3.0-or-later, dynamically linked by sharp, used by
Next.js), caniuse-lite (CC-BY-4.0 data).
